>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `add_looper`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.add_looper : string * (simpExtLib.simpset -> tactic) ->
  simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds a named looper to an extension simpset.

`add_looper (name, mk) ss` passes the current invocation simpset to `mk`.
Loopers run after rewriting and final solvers leave the goal open. New names
append; an existing name is replaced in place. A looper must fail when
inapplicable (`Conv.UNCHANGED` also counts) and make progress when successful.
`ExclX ("looper:" ^ name)` disables it for one invocation. Bare exclusions
try strict rewrite/dproc lookup before strategy fallback.

### Failure

Never fails at installation.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>>_ val ext_bool_ss = simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss;
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.add_looper ("conj", fn _ => CONJ_TAC)
     ext_bool_ss;
>> simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} ss [] ([], “p ∧ q”) c;
>> simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} ss
     [simpExtLib.ExclX "looper:conj"] ([], “p ∧ q”) c;
```

